/// known-gap: interp has no aspects; the interpreter is being retired
/// `aspect Name |` ... `xx` names a set of fields; a class takes them with
/// `uses Name`. A field written without a value starts at 0.0 when it is a
/// `~` trait and at nil otherwise. A value in the aspect is the starting
/// value; a line the class writes wins over it, and an object's own value
/// wins over both. The aspect may come after the classes that use it. An
/// object that mutates keeps its values; its new class has the fields of
/// the aspects it uses.
<>Tribe |
    uses Political, Wealth
    ~tradition: .7
    transition mutate where @gold >= 10
        into: Village
    xx
xx
<>Village |
    uses Political, Wealth
    granary: 0
xx
aspect Political |
    ~aggression
    ~stability: .5
    ~tradition: .2
xx
aspect Wealth |
    gold: 1
    army
xx
t <> Tribe | aggression: .25
v <> Village | gold: 3
:say("{t >> aggression} {t >> stability} {t >> tradition} {t >> gold} {t >> army}")
:say("{v >> aggression} {v >> stability} {v >> tradition} {v >> gold} {v >> granary}")
t >> gold |= 12
:tick()
:say(:len(:objects(Village)))
